<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
<h2>DQ Onion Rings — What Sets Them Apart</h2>
<p>DQ Onion Rings use thick-cut onion slices in a batter that is thicker than typical fast-food onion rings. The result is a more substantial ring — less about the batter, more about the onion — that holds its structure and crunch for several minutes after serving. Find all DQ snack options on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>
<h2>Onion Rings vs. Regular Fries vs. Cheese Curds — Which to Order?</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Regular Fries</td><td class="price-cell">$2.49+</td><td>260+ cal</td><td>Best value, lightest, included in meal deals</td></tr><tr><td>Onion Rings</td><td class="price-cell">$3.29+</td><td>400+ cal</td><td>More indulgent, thick-cut, best as snack</td></tr><tr><td>Cheese Curds</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>470 cal</td><td>Gooey white cheddar, shareable</td></tr><tr><td>Pretzel Sticks + Queso</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>440 cal</td><td>Comfort food, great for sharing</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Are Onion Rings a Good Deal at DQ?</h2>
<p>At $3.29 for a regular order, DQ Onion Rings cost $0.80 more than a small Regular Fries but deliver 140 extra calories and a significantly more indulgent snack experience. They are not in the $7 Meal Deal or any standard combo — they are an à la carte upgrade. If you are adding a side to a burger or basket, Regular Fries are the value play. If you want something more interesting and shareable, Onion Rings or Cheese Curds are worth the premium.</p>
<h2>What Dipping Sauces Pair Best with DQ Onion Rings?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Ranch</strong> — The most popular pairing. Creamy and cool against the crispy, savory ring.</li>
  <li><strong>Zesty Queso</strong> — If you order Onion Rings and Pretzel Sticks together, the queso doubles as a great onion ring dip.</li>
  <li><strong>Honey Mustard</strong> — Sweet-tangy, a classic onion ring pairing.</li>
</ul>
